{
  "id": "S2E18",
  "season": 2,
  "episode": 18,
  "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
  "title": "Honestly",
  "dates": "Sunday, February 21 – Wednesday, February 24, 2010",
  "logline": "The First Sunday of Lent and a phone that doesn’t ring; a professor who can’t help himself; and on Tuesday, a porch light left on, a dinner for two, and a promise kept to her face.",
  "previously": [
    {
      "text": "On the levee, Lena: “In my wallet.” … “It’s his. He reads it first.” … “Sunday,” … “After Mass. To his face, when we’re both back.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "In his office, Hale: “You’re both at your very best with an audience, which is most of what’s wrong with you.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "In the darkroom, Skye: “When you come back,” … “Whatever you’ve got. Whatever happens down there — the Saints, Mardi Gras, a float falls on you. You tell me. To my face.”",
      "if": "promised_skye_truth"
    },
    {
      "text": "At a pump in Blythe, Skye: “Del Playa. Six. I’ll leave the porch light on.” … “Don’t eat. I’m making you dinner. I’ve never made anybody dinner.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Past Sonora, Theo: “Be good to her,” … “Tuesday. Just — be good to her.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "In his office, Father Osei: “For your penance,” … “On Tuesday, before you go to her door, say an Our Father for her. Slowly.” … “For her. Not for you.”"
    }
  ],
